From: kadie@eff.org (Carl M. Kadie)
Newsgroups: comp.admin.policy,alt.comp.acad-freedom.talk
Subject:  Re: Policy from the Stevens Institute of Technology login
Date: 8 Nov 1993 19:19:06 -0500
Message-ID: <2bmnlq$iih@eff.org>

Comments from someone at Stevens:

[...]
Note that at SIT, mere possession of "phony mail" programs is a crime, and
computer accounts are suspended before any hearings in the case of chain mail.
[...]
(FWIW, the Network Review Board is viewed by some on campus as a mere puppet
of the Computer Center, and not an autonomous group. But that's another story.)
[...]

[Two additional notes:]

>>        ANTI-WATCHDOG programs are prohibited on the VAXcluster.
 

The Watchdog (according to the Computer Center) only watches for processes
that have been idle for XX minutes and logs them out.  The reasons are (1) to
free up the processors and (2) to eliminate the possible use of an account that
was inadvertantly left logged without the account holder being present.


>>++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
>>Sending electronic mail or messages to other users at Stevens (or elsewhere)
>>UNDER A PHONEY USERNAME is not permitted.  Having mail-sending programs which 
>>falsify the sender's identity is also not allowed since this type of program 
>>is only "useful" for sending phoney mail.  
>>++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++

What about anonymous remailers?

